**When to read this file:** When you add or gate code that touches files, network, OS, hardware, UI, or security — and always when you edit `std/src/ooda/` (see `BOOTSTRAP.oot` tier *Security, sandboxing, capability gating* + `DESIGN.oot` §3).

*Update this list when a token is added or fractured. Keep count note in sync with DESIGN. Prefer granular tokens in new APIs. CAP-G1 net preferred-map is path-A in check + runtime require (legacy NetCap supersede); do **not** claim full OS isolation or that non-net CAP-G* families are done.*
